: \"National Reporting System for Adult Education, 2015-16\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The National Reporting System for Adult Education, 2015-16 (NRS 2015-16), is part of the Adult Education and Family Literacy program; program data is available since 1997 at <https://wdcrobcolp01.ed.gov/CFAPPS/OVAE/NRS/login.cfm>. NRS 2015-16 (http://www.nrsweb.org) is a cross-sectional study that is designed to monitor performance accountability for the federally funded, state-administered adult education program. States will be required to submit their progress in adult education and literacy activities by reporting data on core indicators of outcomes on all adult learners who receive 12 or more hours of service as well as state expenditures on the adult education program. States can also report on additional, optional secondary measures that include outcomes related to employment, family, and community. The study will be conducted using a web-based reporting system of states. NRS 2015-16 is a universe survey, and all states are expected to submit data. Key statistics that will be produced from the study include student demographics, receipt of secondary school diploma or general education development (GED) certificate, placement in postsecondary education or training, educational gain, and employment placement and retention.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Annual Performance Report\", \"Financial Reports\", \"OVAE's GPRA goals for adult education\", \"Adult literacy\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2016-06-27\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Office of Career, Technical, and Adult Education\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Joshua Behsudi\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:joshua.behsudi@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"OCTAE_2016001\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:30\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2015/2016\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://wdcrobcolp01.ed.gov/CFAPPS/OVAE/NRS/login.cfm\",\r\n          \"description\": \"National Reporting System for Adult Education, 2015-16 data available through the Office of Career, Technical, and Adult Education (OCTAE) National Reporting System (NRS) application\",\r\n          \"title\": \"OCTAE NRS Application\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P1Y\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"http://www.nrsweb.org\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"National Reporting System for Adult Education, 2016-17\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The National Reporting System for Adult Education, 2016-17 (NRS 2016-17), is part of the Adult Education and Family Literacy program; program data is available since 1997 at <https://wdcrobcolp01.ed.gov/CFAPPS/OVAE/NRS/login.cfm>. NRS 2016-17 (http://www.nrsweb.org) is a cross-sectional study that is designed to monitor performance accountability for the federally funded, state-administered adult education program. States will be required to submit their progress in adult education and literacy activities by reporting data on core indicators of outcomes on all adult learners who receive 12 or more hours of service as well as state expenditures on the adult education program. States can also report on additional, optional secondary measures that include outcomes related to employment, family, and community. The study will be conducted using a web-based reporting system of states. NRS 2016-17 is a universe survey, and all states are expected to submit data. Key statistics that will be produced from the study include student demographics, receipt of secondary school diploma or general education development (GED) certificate, placement in postsecondary education or training, educational gain, and employment placement and retention.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Annual Performance Report\", \"Financial Reports\", \"OVAE's GPRA goals for adult education\", \"Adult literacy\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2016-06-27\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Office of Career, Technical, and Adult Education\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Joshua Behsudi\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:joshua.behsudi@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"OCTAE_2017001\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:30\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2016/2017\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://wdcrobcolp01.ed.gov/CFAPPS/OVAE/NRS/login.cfm\",\r\n          \"description\": \"National Reporting System for Adult Education, 2016-17 data available through the Office of Career, Technical, and Adult Education (OCTAE) National Reporting System (NRS) application\",\r\n          \"title\": \"OCTAE NRS Application\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P1Y\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"http://www.nrsweb.org\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Annual Submission of Financial Statements and Compliance Audits, 2012-13\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The Annual Submission of Financial Statements and Compliance Audits, 2012-13 (ASFS 2012-13), is a study that is part of the Annual Submission of Financial Statements and Compliance Audits program. ASFS 2012-13 is a cross-sectional survey that collects data from postsecondary institutions in the form of annual audited financial statements. The study was conducted using a web-based data collection system where postsecondary institutions submitted information. The universe of postsecondary schools was sampled. The study's response rate was 100 percent. Key statistics produced from ASFS 2012-13 are on the disbursement of Title IV funding, compliance to federal regulations regarding Title IV funding, and overall financial health of institutions.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Postsecondary institutions\", \"Public\", \"Private\", \"Non-profit\", \"Not-for-profit\", \"For-profit\", \"Proprietary\", \"Financial statements\", \"Compliance audits\", \"Federal Student Aid\", \"FSA\", \"Title IV\", \"Higher Education Act\", \"HEA\", \"Finances\", \"Loans\", \"Grants\", \"Proprietary school 90/10 revenue percentages\", \"School Participation Division\", \"eZ-Audit\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2015-06-29\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Office of Federal Student Aid\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Ti Baker\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:ti.baker@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"FSA_2013009\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:45\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2013/P1Y\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://studentaid.ed.gov/sa/about/data-center/school/composite-scores\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Section 498(c) of the Higher Education Act of 1965, as amended, requires for-profit and non-profit institutions to annually submit audited financial statements to the Department to demonstrate they are maintaining the standards of financial responsibility necessary to participate in the Title IV programs. One of many standards, which the Department utilizes to gauge the financial responsibility of an institution, is a composite of three ratios derived from an institution's audited financial statements. The three ratios are a primary reserve ratio, an equity ratio, and a net income ratio. These ratios gauge the fundamental elements of the financial health of an institution, not the educational quality of an institution.\",\r\n          \"title\": \"Financial Responsibility Composite Scores\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://studentaid.ed.gov/sa/about/data-center/school/proprietary\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Section 487(d)(4) of the Higher Education Act of 1965 (HEA), as amended, requires the Secretary to annually submit a report to Congress containing information regarding the amount and percentage of each proprietary institution's revenues from Title IV sources and non-Title IV sources as provided by the institution in its audited financial statements. The reports are sent to the Chairmen and Ranking Members of the corresponding House and Senate authorizing committees. Below, you can access the 90/10 transmittal letters, summary charts and reports for institutions with fiscal years ending in the corresponding award year.\",\r\n          \"title\": \"Proprietary School 90/10 Revenue Percentages\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"issued\": \"2014-07-22\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://ezaudit.ed.gov/EZWebApp/default.do\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 1993, Base Year\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 1993, Base Year (B&B:93) is part of the Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study (B&B) program. B&B:93 (https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/b&b/) is a base year of a longitudinal study that followed a cohort of graduating college seniors who participated in the 1993 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:93). The 1993 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:93) data provided the base-year sample for B&B:93. NPSAS:93 data are representative of all undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in postsecondary institutions in the 50 United States, the District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico that were eligible to participate in the federal financial aid programs in Title IV of the Higher Education Act, and the B&B cohorts is a representative sample of graduating seniors in all majors. Key statistics produced from B&B:93 are information on bachelor’s degree recipients’ undergraduate experience, demographic backgrounds, expectations regarding graduate study and work, and participation in community service.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Postsecondary education and training\", \"Labor market outcomes\", \"Family formation\", \"Longitudinal\", \"Undergraduate experience\", \"Bachelor's degree\", \"Employment\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2005-09-01\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Ted Socha\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:ted.socha@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2006166\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"1992/2003\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/datalab/postsecondary/index.aspx\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study, 1993 data available through PowerStats in the NCES Datalab\",\r\n          \"format\": \"API\",\r\n          \"title\": \"PowerStats\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=96147\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Public use data system for the Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study, 1993 base year and first follow-up (1994)\",\r\n          \"title\": \"CD-ROM: Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study First Follow-up DAS\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2000158\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Public use data system for the Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study, 1993 base year through second follow-up (1997)\",\r\n          \"title\": \"CD-ROM: Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study Second Follow-up B&B:93/97: Public Use Data Analysis System (DAS)\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2005150\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Public use data system for the Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study, 1993 third follow-up (2003)\",\r\n          \"title\": \"Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 1993/2003 Data Analysis System (DAS) On-line\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"irregular\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"issued\": \"1996-09-30\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/b&b/\",\r\n      \"references\": [ \"https://nces.ed.gov/datalab/powerstats/pdf/bb03_varname.pdf\" ],\r\n      \"systemOfRecords\": \"https://www2.ed.gov/notices/pai/pai-18-13-01.pdf\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 2000, Base Year\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 2000, Base Year (B&B:2000) is part of the Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study (B&B) program. B&B:2000 (https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/b&b/) is a base year of a longitudinal study that followed a cohort of graduating college seniors who participated in the 2000 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:2000). The 2000 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:2000) data provided the base-year sample for B&B:2000. NPSAS:2000 data are representative of all undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in postsecondary institutions in the 50 United States, the District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico that were eligible to participate in the federal financial aid programs in Title IV of the Higher Education Act, and the B&B cohort is a representative sample of graduating seniors in all majors. Key statistics produced from B&B:2000 are information on bachelor’s degree recipients’ undergraduate experience, demographic backgrounds, expectations regarding graduate study and work, and participation in community service.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Postsecondary education and training\", \"Labor market outcomes\", \"Family formation\", \"Longitudinal\", \"Undergraduate experience\", \"Bachelor's degree\", \"Employment\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2003-08-15\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Ted Socha\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:ted.socha@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2003156\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"1999/2001\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"description\": \"2000 Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study data available through on-line Data Analysis System\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2003174\",\r\n          \"title\": \"Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 2000/01 Data Analysis System (DAS) On-line\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P8Y\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"issued\": \"2003-08-27\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 2008, Base Year\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study 2008, Base Year (B&B:08) is part of the Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study (B&B) program. B&B:08 (https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/b&b/) is a base year of a longitudinal study that followed a cohort of graduating college seniors who participated in the 2008 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:08). The 2008 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:08) data provided the base-year sample for B&B:08. NPSAS:08 data are representative of all undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in postsecondary institutions in the 50 United States, the District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico that were eligible to participate in the federal financial aid programs in Title IV of the Higher Education Act, and the B&B cohort is a representative sample of graduating seniors in all majors. Key statistics produced from B&B:08 are information on bachelor’s degree recipients’ undergraduate experience, demographic backgrounds, expectations regarding graduate study and work, and participation in community service.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Postsecondary education and training\", \"Labor market outcomes\", \"Family formation\", \"Longitudinal\", \"Undergraduate experience\", \"Bachelor's degree\", \"Employment\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2012-03-15\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Ted Socha\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:ted.socha@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2011236\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"restricted public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2007/2012\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/datalab/postsecondary/index.aspx\",\r\n          \"title\": \"Datalab for Postsecondary Education\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"description\": \"2008-09 Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study: Restricted-Use First Follow-up Data Files and File Documentation\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2012245\",\r\n          \"title\": \"2008-09 Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study: Restricted-Use First Follow-up Data Files and File Documentation\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"description\": \"2008-12 Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study (B&B:08/12) restricted-use data files\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2014641rev\",\r\n          \"title\": \"2008-12 Baccalaureate and Beyond Longitudinal Study (B&B:08/12) restricted-use data files\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P8Y\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"issued\": \"2014-07-14\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/B&B/\",\r\n      \"systemOfRecords\": \"https://www2.ed.gov/notices/pai/pai-18-13-01.pdf \"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study 2004, Base Year\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The 2004 Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study, 2004 Base Year (BPS:04) is part of the Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study (BPS) program. BPS:04 is the base year of a longitudinal study that followed a cohort of students who enrolled in postsecondary education for the first time during the 2003–04 academic year, irrespective of date of high school completion. The 2003–04 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:04) data provided the base-year sample for BPS:04. BPS:04 data are representative of all first time beginning students (FTB) enrolled in postsecondary institutions in the 50 United States, the District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico that were eligible to participate in the federal financial aid programs of Title IV of the Higher Education Act. Key statistics produced from the BPS:04 are issues as persistence and the effects of financial aid on subsequent enrollment. The cohort includes a sample of 23,090 students, a subset of students initially sampled for participation in NPSAS:04 and classified by their NPSAS institution as FTBs.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Postsecondary education\", \"Educational attainment\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2011-03-08\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"David Richards\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:david.richards@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2007169\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2003/2009\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/datalab/postsecondary/index.aspx\",\r\n          \"title\": \"Datalab for Postsecondary Education\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2012243\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Restricted-Use Transcript Data Files and Documentation for 2004/2009 Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study\",\r\n          \"title\": \"2004/2009 Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study Restricted-Use Transcript Data Files and Documentation\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2011244\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Restricted-use data file for 2004/2009 Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study\",\r\n          \"title\": \"2004/2009 Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study Restricted-Use Data File\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"irregular\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/bps/\",\r\n      \"systemOfRecords\": \"https://www2.ed.gov/notices/pai/pai-18-13-01.pdf\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study 2012, Base Year\",\r\n      \"description\":\"The 2012 Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study, 2012 Base Year (BPS:12) is part of the Beginning Postsecondary Students Longitudinal Study (BPS) program. BPS:12 is the base year of a longitudinal study that followed a cohort of students who enrolled in postsecondary education for the first time during the 2011–12 academic year, irrespective of date of high school completion. The 2012–13 National Postsecondary Student Aid Study (NPSAS:12) data provided the base-year sample for BPS:12. BPS:12 data are representative of all first-time beginning (FTB) students enrolled in postsecondary institutions in the 50 United States and the District of Columbia that were eligible to participate in the federal financial aid programs in Title IV of the Higher Education Act. The cohort includes a subset of students initially sampled for participation in NPSAS:12 and classified by their NPSAS institution as FTBs. Key statistics produced from BPS:12 are data on student persistence in, and completion of, postsecondary education programs; their transition to employment; demographic characteristics; and changes over time in their goals, marital status, income, and debt, among other measures.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Postsecondary education\", \"Educational 