ion centers functioning as LEAs were sampled. Prior to 2011-12, charter schools were primarily sampled if they were part of a LEA, not if they were a separate charter school district. For CRDC 2009-10, 100% of LEAs and 100% of schools provided data. Key statistics produced from CRDC 2009-10 can provide information about critical civil rights issues as well as contextual information on the state of civil rights in the nation, including enrollment demographics, advanced placement, discipline, and special education services.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Elementary and secondary education\", \"Civil rights\", \"Discrimination\", \"Schools\", \"Students\", \"Education of students with disabilities\", \"Sex discrimination\", \"Minority groups\", \"Special education services\", \"Student discipline\", \"Mental retardation\", \"Graduation testing\", \"Student pregnancy\", \"Advanced placement\", \"Enrollment demographics\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2012-03-07\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Office for Civil Rights\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Janis Brown\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:Janis.Brown@ED.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"OCR_2011001\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:00\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2009/2010\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"a