t the same school, moved to another school, or left the profession in the year following the Schools and Staffing Survey (SASS) administration.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Teacher attrition\", \"Movers\", \"Leavers\", \"Stayers\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2016-10-06\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Amy Ho\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:amy.ho@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2014077\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2012/2013\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2014356\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Restricted-use data file for the 2011-12 School and Staffing Survey\",\r\n          \"title\": \"2011-12 Schools and Staffing Survey (SASS) Restricted-Use Data Files\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P2Y\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/sass/index.asp\",\r\n      \"systemOfRecords\": \"https://www2.ed.gov/notices/pai/pai-18-13-01.pdf\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Principal Follow-Up Survey, 2012-13\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The 2012-13 Principal Follow-Up Survey (PFS 12/13) is a longitudinal follow-up to the 2011-12 Schools and Staffing Survey (SASS 11-12) study. PFS 12/13 (https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/sass/) determined how many principals remained at the same school, moved to another school, or left the profession in the year following the 2011-12 Schools and Staffing Survey (SASS 11-12) administration. PFS 12/13 was administered to a sample of principals who completed the SASS 11-12 principal questionnaire. Due to its brevity and lack of skip patterns, PFS 12/13 was primarily a mail-based data collection with telephone and email follow-up.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Principal turnover\", \"Principal retention\", \"Principal attrition rates\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2016-10-06\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Amy Ho\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:amy.ho@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2014064REV\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2012/2013\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2014356\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Restricted-use data file for the 2011-12 School and Staffing Survey\",\r\n          \"title\": \"2011-12 Schools and Staffing Survey (SASS) Restricted-Use Data Files\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P2Y\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/sass/index.asp\",\r\n      \"systemOfRecords\": \"https://www2.ed.gov/notices/pai/pai-18-13-01.pdf\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"NCES-Barron's Admissions Competitiveness Index Data Files: 1972, 1982, 1992, 2004, 2008, 2014\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The NCES−Barron’s Admissions Competitiveness Index Data Files: 1972, 1982, 1992, 2004, 2008, 2014 (NCES 2015-332) contain the Barron’s college admissions competitiveness selectivity ratings for 1972, 1982, 1992, 2004, 2008, 2014 along with the NCES Higher Education Information System (HEGIS) FICE ID and Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS) UNITID codes and the Office of Postsecondary Education OPEID codes of each postsecondary institution included. Also included are the city and state of each institution included in the Barron’s lists. The years selected correspond to the years that students in the longitudinal studies (NLS-72, HS&B, NELS:88, ELS-2000,HSLS:09, and BPS) initially attended the 4-year postsecondary institutions. Each of the six NCES−Barron’s index files is available in a separate worksheet in an Excel workbook file that is in Excel 1997–2003 compatible format.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Educational goals\", \"Educational research\", \"Higher education\", \"Access and choice in higher education\", \"Higher education institutions\", \"Postsecondary education\", \"Postsecondary education transcript studies\", \"Postsecondary institutions\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2017-01-10\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"National Center for Education Statistics\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Institute of Education Sciences\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n            \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n              \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n              \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n            }\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Carl M. Schmitt\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:carl.schmitt@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"NCES_2016332\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"restricted public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:50\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"1972/2014\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessUrl\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2016332\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Restricted-use data file for the NCES-Barron's Admissions Competitiveness Index Data Files: 1972, 1982, 1992, 2004, 2008, 2014\",\r\n          \"title\": \"NCES-Barron's Admissions Competitiveness Index Data Files: 1972, 1982, 1992, 2004, 2008, 2014\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"irregular\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Civil Rights Data Collection, 2013-14\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The Civil Rights Data Collection, 2013-14 (CRDC 2013-14) is part of the Civil Rights Data Collection (CRDC) program; program data is available since 2000 at <http://ocrdata.ed.gov/>. CRDC 2013-14 (http://ocrdata.ed.gov/) is a cross-sectional survey that collects data on key education and civil rights issues in the nation's public schools, which include student enrollment and educational programs and services, disaggregated by race/ethnicity, sex, limited English proficiency, and disability. LEAs submit administrative records about schools in the district. CRDC 2013-14 is a universe survey. Key statistics produced from CRDC 2013-14 can provide information about critical civil rights issues as well as contextual information on the state of civil rights in the nation, including enrollment demographics, advanced placement, school discipline, and special education services.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Elementary and secondary education\", \"Civil rights\", \"Discrimination\", \"Schools\", \"Students\", \"Education of students with disabilities\", \"Sex discrimination\", \"Minority groups\", \"Special education services\", \"Student discipline\", \"Mental retardation\", \"Graduation testing\", \"Student pregnancy\", \"Advanced placement\", \"Enrollment demographics\",\"SAT or ACT test participation\", \"Gifted and talented programs\", \"Course-taking\", \"School staff\", \"Sworn law enforcement officers\", \"Teacher experience\", \"School counselors\", \"Teacher certification\", \"Teacher absenteeism\", \"Student chronic absenteeism\", \"Student retention\", \"School expenditures\", \"Juvenile justice facilities\" ],\r\n      \"modified\": \"2017-05-19\",\r\n      \"publisher\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Office for Civil Rights\",\r\n        \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n          \"name\": \"U.S. Department of Education\",\r\n          \"subOrganizationOf\": {\r\n            \"@type\": \"org:Organization\",\r\n            \"name\": \"U.S. Government\"\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"contactPoint\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"vcard:Contact\",\r\n        \"fn\": \"Janis Brown\",\r\n        \"hasEmail\": \"mailto:ocrdata@ed.gov\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"identifier\": \"OCR_2016001\",\r\n      \"accessLevel\": \"public\",\r\n      \"bureauCode\": [ \"018:00\" ],\r\n      \"programCode\": [ \"018:000\" ],\r\n      \"license\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\r\n      \"spatial\": \"United States\",\r\n      \"temporal\": \"2013/2014\",\r\n      \"distribution\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/flex/Reports.aspx?type=school\",\r\n          \"description\": \"View and compare data across multiple schools and districts\",\r\n          \"title\": \"School Search\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/flex/Reports.aspx?type=district\",\r\n          \"description\": \"View and compare data across multiple schools and districts\",\r\n          \"title\": \"District Search\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"accessURL\": \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/DistrictSchoolSearch\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Find school- or district-level summaries; access all data for a single school or district\",\r\n          \"title\": \"School/District Search\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"@type\": \"dcat:Distribution\",\r\n          \"downloadURL\": \"https://inventory.data.gov/dataset/2acc601e-9806-4dff-b144-f8a5e7c095b8/resource/3dc84a95-526a-4b90-aacd-72f60d4fecbc/download/crdc201314csv.zip\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Download the entire 2013-14 Civil Rights Data Collection data file via one .zip file\",\r\n          \"format\": \"Zipped CSV\",\r\n          \"mediaType\": \"application/zip\",\r\n          \"title\": \"crdc201314csv.zip\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"accrualPeriodicity\": \"R/P2Y\",\r\n      \"dataQuality\": true,\r\n      \"issued\": \"2016-06-06\",\r\n      \"language\": [ \"en-US\" ],\r\n      \"landingPage\": \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/\",\r\n      \"references\": [ \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/Overview\", \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/downloads/UserGuide.pdf\", \"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/downloads/FAQ.pdf\",\"https://ocrdata.ed.gov/DataInfor1314\" ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"dcat:Dataset\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Civil Rights Data Collection, 2015-16\",\r\n      \"description\": \"The Civil Rights Data Collection, 2015-16 (CRDC 2015-16) is part of the Civil Rights Data Collection (CRDC) program; program data is available since 2000 at <http://ocrdata.ed.gov/>. CRDC 2015-16 (http://ocrdata.ed.gov/) is a cross-sectional survey that collects data on key education and civil rights issues in the nation's public schools, which include student enrollment and educational programs and services, disaggregated by race/ethnicity, sex, limited English proficiency, and disability. LEAs submit administrative records about schools in the district. CRDC 2015-16 is a universe survey. Key statistics produced from CRDC 2015-16 can provide information about critical civil rights issues as well as contextual information on the state of civil rights in the nation, including enrollment demographics, advanced placement, school discipline, and special education services.\",\r\n      \"keyword\": [ \"Elementary and secondary education\", \"Civil rights\", \"Discrimination\", \"Schools\", \"Students\", \"Education of students with disabilities\", \"Sex discrimination\", \"Minority groups\", \"Special education services\", \"Student discipline\", \"Mental retardation\", \"Graduation testing\", \"Student pregnancy\", \"Advanced placement\", \"Enrollment demographics\" ],\r\n      \